{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","name_native":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"36":"Signet-Rings (Kitab Al-Khatam)"},"section_detail":{"36":{"hadithnumber_first":4214,"hadithnumber_last":4239,"arabicnumber_first":4214,"arabicnumber_last":4239,"name_native":"Signet-Rings (Kitab Al-Khatam)"}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":4214,"arabicnumber":4214,"text":"Narrated Anas bin Malik:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wanted to write to some persian rulers. He was told that they would not read a letter without a seal in the form of a silver ring on which he engraved \"Muhammad the Messenger of Allah","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Shuaib Al Arnaut","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Bukhari (5872)"}],"reference":{"book":36,"hadith":1}}]}